我想认识我的人都知道这一点。

37
00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:17.670
The world knows that.
全世界都知道。

38
00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:18.810
Don't give him my address, please.
请别把我的地址告诉他。

39
00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:19.290
I won't.
我不会的。

40
00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:19.530
Okay.
好的。

41
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.450
Creed's address is – his hidden key is –
克里德的地址是——他藏钥匙的地方是——

42
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.010
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

43
00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.390
Yes, we are neighbors, and it's one of the joys of my life that we're neighbors.
没错，我们是邻居，能成为邻居是我人生中的一大乐事。

44
00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.770
I love that you're right around the corner.
我很高兴你就住在转角处。

45
00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.110
I love that we have –
我很高兴我们有——

46
00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.090
We see each other walking.
我们经常看到对方在散步。

47
00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.070
We see each other walking.
我们经常看到对方在散步。

48
00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:33.670
We see each other hiking around the street.
我们看到对方在街区附近徒步。

49
00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.030
We do.
我们确实会。

50
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:34.510
Hey!
嘿！

51
00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.470
You were walking – was it your daughter's dog?
你当时在遛狗——那是你女儿的狗吗？

52
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:38.070
Your son's dog?
是你儿子的狗？

53
00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.210
My son's a little Yorkie, yeah.
是我儿子的，一只约克夏，没错。

54
00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.030
A little Yorkie, and I hear, hey, pumpkin, and I turn around and it's Creed.
一只小约克夏，然后我听到有人喊“嘿，小南瓜”，我一回头，是克里德。

55
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.990
And we've also maybe had some adult beverage and red solo cups.
而且我们当时可能还喝了点酒，手里拿着红色塑料杯。

56
00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:47.340
We may have.
可能吧。

57
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:47.770
We may have.
可能吧。

58
00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:52.890
And we like to do a little bit of what we call the sauce trail and walk around having a glass of wine.
我们喜欢搞点所谓的“酒精漫步”，就是边散步边喝红酒。

59
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.050
And watching documentaries.
还要看纪录片。

60
00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:58.970
Oh, yeah, Creed loves – anything where, like, animals go crazy, like planet Earth.
噢，没错，克里德超爱看——任何那种动物发疯的片子，比如《地球脉动》之类的。

61
00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:00.170
Yes, all that stuff.
对，就是那些。

62
00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:00.750
I just love it.
我真的超爱。

63
00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:01.110
All right.
好吧。

64
00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:02.850
Well, we are really excited to have you here.
我们真的很高兴你能来。

65
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.110
We are discussing the Halloween episode.
我们正在讨论万圣节那一集。

66
00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:05.790
Yes.
没错。

67
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:06.710
Right, right.
对，对。

68
00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.530
Season 2, Episode 5.
第二季第五集。

69
00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:15.350
This was written by Greg Daniels and directed by Paul Feig, and it is the first episode that Creed speaks.
这一集由格雷格·丹尼尔斯编剧，保罗·费格执导，也是克里德第一次开口说话的一集。

70
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.810
Well, I actually spoke in Diversity Day.
其实我在《多元化日》那集就说过话了。

71
00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.550
In Diversity Day, I had lines with Phyllis.
在《多元化日》里，我和菲利斯有对手戏。

72
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:22.510
Yes, I told her.
没错，我跟她说了。

73
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:27.030
She paid me afterwards, said, well, the first A.D., remember that girl we had the first A.D.?
她事后还付了我钱，她说，那个第一副导演，还记得我们第一季那个第一副导演吗？

74
00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:27.230
Yeah.
记得。

75
00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:27.830
The first season?
第一季的时候？

76
00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.550
She thought I was part of the cast at the time.
她当时以为我是剧组成员。

77
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.230
So she came and we had little hands, and she said, now, you and Phyllis just start talking.
所以她走过来，我们当时在拍小手那个镜头，她说，现在，你和菲利斯开始聊天。

78
00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.150
And Phyllis said, wait.
然后菲利斯说，等等。

79
00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:35.950
I said, never mind.
我说，算了。

80
00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:36.710
It's okay.
没关系。

81
00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:38.830
Never mind.
算了。

82
00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.510
Phyllis was going to out you.
菲利斯当时是想揭穿你吧。

83
00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:41.830
Phyllis was going to out me.
菲利斯是想揭穿我。

84
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:42.510
So I said, never mind.
所以我说，算了。

85
00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:42.970
It's fine.
没事的。

86
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.970
And so we started – and I started talking about, you know, sacrificing goats or something, you know.
然后我们就开始了——我开始聊什么献祭山羊之类的话题，你知道的。

87
00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:48.530
Of course you did.
你当然会聊这个。

88
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.310
Trying to tell her what was on her head.
想告诉她她头上顶着什么东西。

89
00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.190
Your improv was sacrificing goats.
你的即兴发挥居然是献祭山羊。

90
00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.010
Yes, yes, yes.
没错，没错，没错。

91
00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:54.670
So you can hear me in the background.
所以你能在背景音里听到我说话。

92
00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.390
And later on, they said, wait a minute, Creed's talking in the background.
后来他们说，等一下，克里德在背景里说话呢。

93
00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.950
And I said, oh, shoot, how did that happen?
我说，噢，糟了，这怎么发生的？

94
00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.650
Yeah, how'd that happen, Creed?
是啊，这怎么发生的，克里德？

95
00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:06.230
And so they paid me on the side, but they didn't say, but we can't – I said, no, it's fine.
于是他们私下付了我钱，但他们没说，我说，不，没关系。

96
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:06.950
It's fine.
没关系的。

97
00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.370
And then off camera, then I also was the voice for the ride.
而且在镜头外，我还为那个游乐设施配了音。

98
00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.050
Yes, for the mining ride.
没错，就是那个矿车游乐设施。

99
00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.290
For the mining ride, you know.
就是那个矿车游乐设施，你懂的。

100
00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.090
You were so funny.
你当时太搞笑了。

101
00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.910
I think they paid attention to that one.
我觉得他们注意到了那一段。

102
00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:20.150
Yeah, you were so funny as the voice of the mining ride.
是啊，你给矿车游乐设施配音的时候太搞笑了。

103
00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:24.110
And Isabel was watching that episode with me, and she said, mom, I know that voice.
伊莎贝尔当时正和我一起看那一集，她说，妈妈，我认得那个声音。

104
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.090
I know that voice.
我认得那个声音。

105
00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.330
And I was like, wait, you're – oh, my gosh.
我当时就想，等等，你是——天哪。

106
00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.390
She was like, I think it's Creed.
她说，我觉得那是克里德。

107
00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:29.290
She?
她说的？

108
00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:29.990
Oh, yeah.
噢，是的。

109
00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:30.870
How discerning is she?
她眼光真毒啊？

110
00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.790
She is – I mean, I didn't catch it.
她是——我是说，我都没听出来。

111
00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.210
And then I looked it up, and I'm like, Isabel, we do know that voice.
后来我查了一下，我说，伊莎贝尔，我们确实认得那个声音。

112
00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:35.730
It's Creed.
那是克里德。

113
00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:41.990
Yeah, but anyway, this is the first time where I actually had some serious lines.
是啊，不过话说回来，这是我第一次真正有了一些重要的台词。

114
00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.710
It was six and a half pages.
足足有六页半长。

115
00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.170
I remember Ken Zabornik threw the script down.
我记得肯·扎博尼克把剧本扔了下来。

116
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.290
He said, okay, here it is.
他说，好了，就是这个。

117
00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.790
This is your moment.
这是属于你的高光时刻。

118
00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:50.210
Wow.
哇。

119
00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.510
And I had memorized it forwards and backwards.
我把台词背得滚瓜烂熟，正着背反着背都行。

120
00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:58.870
I had set a timer on a little recorder at a night, subliminally at two and three in the morning,
我还在一个小录音机上设了定时，在晚上，潜意识里，在凌晨两三点的时候，

121
00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.970
that would go off and play the lines while I was sleeping.
它就会响起来，在我睡觉的时候播放那些台词。

122
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:02.710
Creep.
变态。

123
00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.150
I had it backwards and forwards.
我把它背得滚瓜烂熟。

124
00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:04.550
No joke.
没开玩笑。

125
00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:05.110
I had it backwards.
我甚至能倒着背。

126
00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:05.170
Wow.
哇。

127
00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.030
I knew this was the Rubicon.
我知道这就是我的卢比孔河。

128
00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.790
This is the place that I was going to get.
这是我即将获得成功的关键点。

129
00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.450
My intuition said, this is it.
我的直觉告诉我，就是现在。

130
00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:16.490
And then, of course, we walk in the office, and Greg, they came in and said, by the way,
然后，当然了，我们走进办公室，格雷格他们进来说，顺便提一下，

131
00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:20.930
we've made changes, of course, to the lines, and we've reversed them around and added some
我们当然对台词做了修改，把顺序打乱了，还加了一些

132
00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:21.290
new stuff.
新内容。

133
00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.590
You're okay, Steve goes, yeah, fine.
你还好吗，史蒂夫说，行，没问题。

134
00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:23.430
I go, oh.
我说，噢。

135
00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.270
Because they used to do that to us all the time.
因为他们以前总是那样对我们。

136
00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:26.690
Oh, all the time.
噢，一直都是这样。

137
00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:30.870
We would come in, and you'd just get new pages and then shoot the scene five minutes later.
我们刚到，就会拿到新剧本，然后五分钟后就要拍那场戏。

138
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.530
Yeah, they would hand you the pages, and sometimes, we've talked about this,
是啊，他们会把剧本递给你，有时候，我们聊过这个，

139
00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:34.550
the pages would be hot.
剧本还是烫手的。

140
00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:36.250
Right off the copier.
刚从复印机里出来。

141
00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:37.150
Right off the copier.
刚从复印机里出来。

142
00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.030
And we'd drop them some.
我们还会掉几页。

143
00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:38.210
Yeah.
是啊。

144
00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.430
Ow, ow, ow, ow.
哎哟，哎哟，哎哟，哎哟。

145
00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:45.750
Now change your lines that you have learned, and you've been having a tape recorder play
现在得改掉你已经背熟的台词，就是那个你还在凌晨三点

146
00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.030
at three in the morning to you.
用录音机放给你听的台词。

147
00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:52.350
Do you remember the backdrop there right off of where my desk and Kate's desk was?
你还记得我办公桌和凯特办公桌后面的那个背景吗？

148
00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.450
And there was the screen there.
那里有个屏风。

149
00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:56.790
And you could sneak around the back and get to the green room from behind it.
你可以从后面溜过去，直接去休息室。

150
00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:57.330
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

151
00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:58.450
That's set up like that.
就是那样安排的。

152
00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:02.450
I walked back like that after they told me this and put my hands up and said, okay, here
他们告诉我这些后，我就是那样走回去的，举起双手说，好吧，就是

153
00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:02.810
it is.
这样。

154
00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.250
And I said, I've come this far.
我说，我都走到这一步了。

155
00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.330
I'm going to do this.
我一定要做这件事。

156
00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:10.070
And once we started, though, with Steve, it was like end of battle, you know?
不过一旦开始和史蒂夫对戏，就像战斗结束了一样，你懂吗？

157
00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:10.610
Yeah.
没错。

158
00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:15.530
And there was some improvisation on that scene because I was paraphrasing my lines because
那场戏里有一些即兴发挥，因为我当时在改写台词，因为

159
00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.190
