00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:57.000
Angela, give us a note card.
安吉拉，给我们一张笔记卡。

651
00:22:57.260 --> 00:22:57.660
All right.
好吧。

652
00:22:57.760 --> 00:23:01.280
At five minutes, 23 seconds, Creed, this is a runner.
在5分23秒处，克里德，这是一个跑龙套的角色。

653
00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:01.740
Oh.
哦。

654
00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:04.900
This is a reference to a runner, but this is a really big deal.
这虽然是个跑龙套的，但这可是件大事。

655
00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:05.360
What?
什么？

656
00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:08.400
Kelly has braided like pigtails.
凯莉扎了像麻花辫一样的发型。

657
00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:08.780
Oh.
哦。

658
00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:09.840
Her hair is down.
她的头发披下来了。

659
00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:10.520
Her hair is down.
她的头发披下来了。

660
00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:11.500
Her hair is down.
她的头发披下来了。

661
00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:12.380
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

662
00:23:12.380 --> 00:23:13.040
It's not in a bun.
没盘成发髻。

663
00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:13.500
I remember.
我记得。

664
00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:18.200
Mindy had a bun for, like, the whole first season, and then about, I guess—
明迪在第一季几乎一直盘着发髻，然后大概——

665
00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:19.120
It was like a twiSt.
那像是个扭转的发髻。

666
00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:19.240
A twiSt.
扭转。

667
00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:20.940
A French twist, I think.
我想是法式盘发。

668
00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:24.000
I mean, she looked—her character really changes her look.
我是说，她看起来——她的角色形象确实变了。

669
00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:26.560
And then she starts having her hair down, and she gets a little sassy.
然后她开始披散头发，变得有点俏皮了。

670
00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:27.700
But this has been a big thing.
但这一直是个大话题。

671
00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.320
We've been wondering, when did they change her hair?
我们一直在想，她们什么时候换的发型？

672
00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:31.180
This is the beginning.
这就是开端。

673
00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:31.940
I see.
我明白了。

674
00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:34.300
I don't think this counts, because it's a Halloween costume.
我觉得这不算，因为那是万圣节装扮。

675
00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:34.780
What?
什么？

676
00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:35.460
Yeah.
是啊。

677
00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:36.580
I'm sorry to say.
很遗憾。

678
00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:37.080
No, no.
不，不。

679
00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:37.500
I agree.
我同意。

680
00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:38.600
I have to say, I'm with Jenna.
我得说，我站珍娜这边。

681
00:23:38.840 --> 00:23:39.300
Thank you.
谢谢。

682
00:23:39.700 --> 00:23:40.180
It doesn't count.
这不算数。

683
00:23:40.360 --> 00:23:42.180
Well, I don't know if I like you here, Creed.
好吧，我不知道我是否喜欢你在这儿，克里德。

684
00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:43.660
All of a sudden, I have someone.
突然之间，我有了支持者。

685
00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:44.360
Oh, well.
哦，好吧。

686
00:23:44.620 --> 00:23:44.940
Tovito.
托维托。

687
00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:50.380
I'm pretty excited, because her hair was down.
我挺兴奋的，因为她的头发披下来了。

688
00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:52.220
Well, but it was a costume, though.
嗯，但那毕竟是装扮。

689
00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:52.390
Oh, my God.
天哪。

690
00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:54.400
It wasn't a regular day in character thing.
那不是角色平时的样子。

691
00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:55.180
That's what I'm saying.
我说的就是这个。

692
00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:55.360
It doesn't apply.
这不作数。

693
00:23:55.360 --> 00:23:56.720
Am I talking to Jenna or Creed?
我是在跟珍娜说话还是跟克里德说话？

694
00:23:56.720 --> 00:23:57.640
I don't know anymore.
我都不清楚了。

695
00:23:57.940 --> 00:23:58.260
It doesn't apply.
这不作数。

696
00:23:58.440 --> 00:23:58.820
All right.
好吧。

697
00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:03.260
You know the scene where Pam and Jim set up a resume for Dwight to get a job someplace else?
你们记得帕姆和吉姆帮德怀特伪造简历让他去别处找工作的那个场景吗？

698
00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:04.960
I have a fan question about that.
我有个关于那个场景的粉丝提问。

699
00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:11.760
RCJH asked, what were you typing on the computer when you and Jim were working on Dwight's resume?
RCJH问，当你和吉姆在写德怀特的简历时，你在电脑上打的是什么？

700
00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:14.120
I was typing what we were saying.
我当时打的就是我们嘴里说的那些话。

701
00:24:14.740 --> 00:24:16.060
Of course you were, Jenna.
你当然是，珍娜。

702
00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:18.380
Of course you were, because you're so method.
你当然是，因为你太入戏了。

703
00:24:18.540 --> 00:24:19.300
I was very method.
我当时确实很入戏。

704
00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:20.540
You're like, I am a responsible person.
你就像是在说，我是一个负责任的人。

705
00:24:20.540 --> 00:24:23.500
You would type out your lines on the computer while you were doing it?
你当时是在一边演一边在电脑上打出台词吗？

706
00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:27.120
Yeah, because Jim would say, I would say, what should we say here?
是啊，因为吉姆会说，我会说，我们这里该说什么呢？

707
00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:30.860
And then he would say what we should say, and I would type it.
然后他会说我们该说什么，我就把它打出来。

708
00:24:31.060 --> 00:24:32.320
And see, here's the thing.
你看，重点是这个。

709
00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.640
I'm very proud of my typing skills.
我对自己打字的技术非常自豪。

710
00:24:34.700 --> 00:24:35.240
Oh, we know.
噢，我们知道。

711
00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:35.640
We know.
我们知道。

712
00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:36.000
Yeah.
是啊。

713
00:24:36.400 --> 00:24:38.380
Creed, do we know or do we know?
克里德，我们是真知道还是假知道？

714
00:24:38.480 --> 00:24:39.500
We really know.
我们是真的知道。

715
00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:39.900
You guys.
你们这些人啊。

716
00:24:39.900 --> 00:24:41.160
Now I'm back on your side, Angela.
现在我又站在你这边了，安吉拉。

717
00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:42.280
Thank you, Creed.
谢谢你，克里德。

718
00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:44.060
Is this how it feels?
这就是那种感觉吗？

719
00:24:44.240 --> 00:24:44.420
Yes.
是的。

720
00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:45.300
Is this how it feels?
这就是那种感觉吗？

721
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:45.580
Yeah.
是啊。

722
00:24:45.740 --> 00:24:46.120
We know.
我们知道。

723
00:24:46.120 --> 00:24:47.920
You'd walk in this thing with just your fingers.
你走进来的时候手指都在动。

724
00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:51.920
We'd be talking about stuff at a craft store, and your fingers would be going like you're typing.
我们在手工店聊天的时候，你的手指就像在打字一样动个不停。

725
00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:53.660
Oh, now that is not true.
噢，那可不是真的。

726
00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:54.260
It was too much.
那太夸张了。

727
00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:54.840
It was too much.
那太夸张了。

728
00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:56.400
Tone it down.
收敛一点。

729
00:24:57.120 --> 00:25:00.660
And then you would tell us about your typing speed and your level of accuracy.
然后你还会跟我们说你的打字速度和准确率。

730
00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:07.940
Well, you should know I was typing our actual lines.
好吧，你们要知道我当时是在打我们真正的台词。

731
00:25:08.020 --> 00:25:09.200
Well, I think that's pretty great, though.
不过我觉得那挺棒的。

732
00:25:09.260 --> 00:25:09.600
Because I can.
因为我能做到。

733
00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:11.880
Because she could, and I can, and I will.
因为她能做到，我也能做到，而且我会去做。

734
00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:12.800
And you're fast, too.
而且你打字也很快。

735
00:25:12.980 --> 00:25:13.340
That's right.
没错。

736
00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:13.840
She's very faSt.
她非常快。

737
00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:24.140
Because Michael's scene with Dwight, when he calls Dwight into his office, and he tells Dwight that he has to fire someone, and Dwight starts naming all the people he should fire.
因为迈克尔和德怀特的那场戏，他把德怀特叫进办公室，告诉德怀特他必须解雇一个人，然后德怀特就开始列举所有他应该解雇的人。

738
00:25:24.140 --> 00:25:32.060
But then Michael implies maybe it should be Dwight, and then Michael's second head starts talking to Dwight.
但后来迈克尔暗示也许应该是德怀特，然后迈克尔的第二个头就开始跟德怀特说话了。

739
00:25:32.580 --> 00:25:32.760
That's right.
没错。

740
00:25:32.760 --> 00:25:37.600
Do you remember Steve and Rain laughing during that scene?
你还记得史蒂夫和雷恩在那场戏里笑场了吗？

741
00:25:37.600 --> 00:25:38.520
Because I do.
因为我记得。

742
00:25:38.520 --> 00:25:40.800
I remember they could not get through that scene.
我记得他们当时根本演不下去那场戏。

743
00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:46.880
I'm sitting out at reception in the background, and they were cracking themselves up in there.
我当时坐在前台的背景里，他们在里面笑得前仰后合。

744
00:25:46.960 --> 00:25:49.060
Rain was literally doubling over.
雷恩简直笑得直不起腰。

745
00:25:49.060 --> 00:25:52.460
Because he was kind of leaning forward, and he would just kind of collapse into himself.
因为他当时身体前倾，然后整个人就缩成了一团。

746
00:25:52.460 --> 00:25:53.620
He was laughing so hard.
他笑得太厉害了。

747
00:25:53.740 --> 00:25:55.840
There must be deleted scenes of that scene.
那场戏一定有删减片段。

748
00:25:55.880 --> 00:25:56.640
Oh, man.
天哪。

749
00:25:56.640 --> 00:25:57.040
I would love to see those.
我真想看看那些片段。

750
00:25:57.040 --> 00:25:57.980
I would love to see that.
我真想看看那个。

751
00:25:58.080 --> 00:25:58.240
Yeah.
是啊。

752
00:25:58.360 --> 00:25:59.440
That is a funny scene.
那场戏真有意思。

753
00:25:59.620 --> 00:26:01.820
Well, Paul Feig called in when we did Office Olympics,
保罗·费格在我们拍《办公室奥运会》时打过电话来，

754
00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:09.100
and he said one of the things he loved about directing episodes of our shows is that you could really find a shot that was cool,
他说他执导我们剧集时最喜欢的一点就是，你可以真正找到一个很酷的镜头，

755
00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:13.000
and you would have the support of Greg to just kind of go with it.
而且格雷格会支持你随性发挥。

756
00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:22.020
And he sort of found that shot where Dwight as the Sith Lord has his, like, hood kind of like – it looks like it's straight out of the movie, you know?
他当时就找到了那个镜头，德怀特扮成西斯大帝，戴着兜帽，看起来就像电影里走出来的一样，你懂吗？

757
00:26:22.220 --> 00:26:22.400
Yes.
没错。

758
00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:23.800
And they just loved that.
他们特别喜欢那个镜头。

759
00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:24.780
The shot from the side, right?
侧面的那个镜头，对吧？

760
00:26:24.780 --> 00:26:25.600
Yeah, shot from the side.
对，侧面的镜头。

761
00:26:25.600 --> 00:26:25.720
Yeah.
没错。

762
00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:31.480
And they sort of just found that and went with it, and Greg was totally supportive of it, and Paul was talking about, like,
他们就是发现了那个镜头并采用了它，格雷格完全支持，保罗当时就在说，

763
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:35.820
how fun that was to have that creative freedom and find those little nuggets.
拥有这种创作自由并挖掘出那些小亮点是多么有趣。

764
00:26:35.820 --> 00:26:37.160
And it's so cool looking.
而且看起来真的很酷。

765
00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:38.860
We had a lot of shots like that.
我们有很多那样的镜头。

766
00:26:38.940 --> 00:26:42.200
They just weren't the cookie-cutter or stereotype, you know, sitcom stuff.
它们不是那种千篇一律的、刻板的情景喜剧套路，你懂的。

767
00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:43.920
And we'd get interesting shots at times.
我们有时会拍到很有趣的镜头。

768
00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:44.160
Yeah.
是啊。

769
00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:46.020
Because all the cameramen were so great.
因为所有的摄影师都太棒了。

770
00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:50.880
And something that we haven't talked about on the show yet is the idea of actor marks.
还有一点我们节目里还没聊过，就是演员站位标记的概念。

771
00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:58.660
So usually on a television show, so that they can get these shots, they put a little piece of tape on the ground.
通常在电视剧拍摄中，为了拍到这些镜头，他们会在地上贴一小块胶带。

772
00:26:58.660 --> 00:27:05.800
And if you – for example, if Jim had to walk up to Pam's desk, there would be a little mark on the ground, and he would have to stand exactly on that mark.
比如，如果吉姆要走到帕姆的办公桌前，地上会有一个小标记，他必须准确地站在那个标记上。

773
00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:07.020
And it's really hard to do.
这真的很难做到。

774
00:27:07.140 --> 00:27:08.360
I mean, do you guys find it hard to do?
我是说，你们觉得这很难吗？

775
00:27:08.360 --> 00:27:14.060
I'm always – I feel like I'm always looking down for the tape, and then I get to my spot, and I look up.
我总是觉得我一直在低头找胶带，走到位置后才抬头。

776
00:27:14.120 --> 00:27:15.820
It's, like, a hard thing to manage.
这真的很难掌控。

777
00:27:16.200 --> 00:27:17.960
Well, on our show, we did not have that.
但在我们的剧里，我们没有那个。

778
00:27:18.080 --> 00:27:18.140
No.
没有。

779
00:27:18.140 --> 00:27:19.780
It would just let us wander.
他们就让我们随意走动。

780
00:27:19.920 --> 00:27:23.640
They would say, just walk up in this general area, and the camera will find you.
他们会说，只要走到这个大概区域就行，摄像机会跟着你。

781
00:27:23.800 --> 00:27:23.920
Yeah.
没错。

782
00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:26.740
It was so loosey-goosey, so amazing.
那种感觉太自由、太棒了。

783
00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:30.460
Didn't you say you were in a band called Loosey-goosey?
你刚才是不是说你以前有个乐队叫“Loosey-goosey”？

784
00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:32.220
I was in a band called Loosey-goosey.
我确实有个乐队叫“Loosey-goosey”。

785
00:27:32.320 --> 00:27:32.500
What?
什么？

786
00:27:32.600 --> 00:27:33.420
I was in a band.
我以前确实有个乐队。

787
00:27:33.420 --> 00:27:33.980
You were not.
你才没有。

788
00:27:34.140 --> 00:27:38.260
With Peter White, who used to play with Al Stewart, and he probably still does.
和彼得·怀特一起，他以前给阿尔·斯图尔特伴奏，可能现在还在伴奏。

789
00:27:38.480 --> 00:27:50.200
We had a band with Dave Camp on sax, and I remember we played the wrap party for this movie I did with – worked on with Bo Bridges at the beach house at Lloyd Bridges' house.
我们还有个乐队，戴夫·坎普吹萨克斯，我记得我们为我拍的一部电影举办杀青派对时演奏过，那部电影是和博·布里奇斯合作的，在劳埃德·布里奇斯的沙滩别墅里。

790
00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:51.280
Loosey-goosey.
Loosey-goosey。

791
00:27:51.440 --> 00:27:55.560
We played out there, and they were dancing out there like Annette Funicello in the surf and stuff.
我们在那儿演奏，他们在那儿跳舞，就像安妮特·弗尼塞洛在冲浪时那样。

792
00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:56.520
Loosey-goosey.
Loosey-goosey。

793
00:27:56.520 --> 00:27:57.320
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

794
00:27:57.760 --> 00:28:01.280
Creed, we just need you to just sit here and tell us about all your stories.
克里德，我们只需要你坐在这儿，给我们讲讲你的所有故事。

795
00:28:01.460 --> 00:28:03.160
Creed, you have literally the most interesting life.
克里德，你的生活简直太有趣了。

796
00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:04.540
I have a fan question for you.
我有一个粉丝提问要问你。

797
00:28:04.540 --> 00:28:05.460
I'm a fascinating character.
我确实是个迷人的人物。

798
00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:06.640
You are.
你确实是。

799
00:28:06.700 --> 00:28:07.340
And humble, too.
而且还很谦虚。

800
00:28:08.540 --> 00:28:13.220
This is a fan question from Todd Myers, and this feels like a good place to ask it.
这是一个来自托德·迈尔斯的粉丝提问，我觉得现在问这个问题正合适。

801
00:28:13.340 --> 00:28:17.800
Who is the biggest rock star you ever partied with during your touring days?
在你巡演的日子里，你参加过派对的最大牌摇滚明星是谁？

802
00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:18.380
Oh.
噢。

803
00:28:19.560 --> 00:28:20.040
Wow.
哇。

804
00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:22.100
It maybe doesn't have to be the biggeSt.
其实不一定非得是最大牌的。

805
00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:23.680
It's just what's the most interesting.
最有趣的那位就行。

806
00:28:23.680 --> 00:28:31.820
I lived for a while at the Camrose Highland Estates, and Linda Ronstadt was there.
我有一段时间住在坎罗斯高地庄园，琳达·朗丝黛当时也在那儿。

807
00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:33.520
Laura Nero was there.
劳拉·尼罗也在那儿。

